<p id="A3.SS1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">and therefore <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{Spec}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})\subseteq[-1/2,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Spec}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})\subseteq[-1/2,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence
<math id="A3.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{1}{2}I\,\preceq\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.428em">⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{1}{2}I\,\preceq\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Together with (<a href="#A3.E4" title="Equation C.4 ‣ Proof of . ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>), this proves
(<a href="#A2.E14" title="Equation B.14 ‣ Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.14</span></a>).</span></p>